The Fall Quarter is upon us, and we are starting our weekly work-sessions this week. Our meeting/worksessions this quarter will be Thursdays 10am -- 12pm, in 360 Shields Library (the DSI <http://dsi.ucdavis.edu/>).

Our work-sessions are open to any/all who have questions about using R, or who want some dedicated space to work for a few hours. Just learning? Come visit! We'll do our best to answer your questions. Plus you can always email the list-serv and generally get an answer. Check our website <http://d-rug.github.io> for more resources

We have a few talks scheduled this quarter, thanks to speakers for volunteering their time. Tentatively the fall quarter schedule is as follows (all from 10-12). We'll try to webcast the talks as well, and recordings will be available on the website.
Oct 26: Brandon Hurr - "Using purrr::map/map2/pmap and the walk family"
Nov 2: Rich Pauloo - "R Markdown Basics: share code and visualizations online, create a CV, build a personal website, and more!"
Nov 16: Kate Tiedeman - "Using R for geospatial research"
Thanks and look forward to seeing you all throughout the quarter.

Adios,
Ryan

